       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and the dose is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day, so the confirmation doesn't change my answer.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the label right away.** For example, metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or 1,000 mg PO twice daily (2,000 mg/day).\n- **Add a note to the order.** It could say that a higher dose is under review under a protocol, so the team can follow up.\n\nIf a protocol really does call for this dose, it should go through your pharmacy or prescriber override process. That process can document the approval and enter the order directly. Tell me if you'd like me to enter one of the in-label doses in the meantime."
      }
